GATE="_synthetic"
EXPECT_EXIT="2"
DESCRIPTION="gate_scanned called with an empty string. The vacuity test lived in an if condition, where a failure is invisible to both errexit and the ERR trap: bash printed 'integer expression expected' to stderr, skipped the body, and the gate passed. An empty denominator is precisely the case the vacuity rule exists for, and it was the one case that slipped through it."
